import { select as $ } from './dom.js';
import { ENEMY_ROLES } from '../enemy-behaviors.js';
import { impactMode, toggleImpactMode } from '../impact-preferences.js';

export function createManual({ modal, syncImpactMode }) {
  function showManual() {
    modal(
      `<h2>Pilot manual</h2><div class="impact-setting"><button class="button secondary" id="manualImpactMode">IMPACT EFFECTS: ${impactMode().toUpperCase()} [V]</button><p>Full adds oversized cel explosions, melee impact arcs, camera punches, armor sparks and directional incoming-hit feedback. Reduced removes camera motion, speed lines, armor flashes and cockpit cracks while keeping the damage direction, armor-hit readout and combat audio. Press V in combat to switch. Your system motion preference is respected until you choose a mode.</p></div><div class="manual-controls"><span><kbd>LEFT CLICK</kbd> Use left hand · hold</span><span><kbd>RIGHT CLICK</kbd> Use right hand · hold</span><span><kbd>W A S D</kbd> Move · automatic boost</span><span><kbd>MOUSE</kbd> Aim continuously</span><span><kbd>Q / MIDDLE MOUSE</kbd> Strafe · hold heading</span><span><kbd>SPACE</kbd> Fly · hold</span><span><kbd>E</kbd> Special</span><span><kbd>SHIFT</kbd> Dash · 3s recharge</span><span><kbd>1 / 2 / 3</kbd> Choose field upgrade</span><span><kbd>F</kbd> Open cache / link relay</span><span><kbd>B</kbd> Field inventory</span><span><kbd>U</kbd> Release cursor for upgrades</span></div><p>Equip any gun, melee weapon, or shield in either hand. Both hands can act at once and recover independently. There is no weapon cycling or zoom. Hold the button for repeated fire or melee attacks; release to lower a shield. All thrust is unlimited. Mouse movement always aims, including without mouse capture. Hold Q or the middle mouse button to lock your movement heading while aiming freely; release to follow your aim again. At the edge of the battlefield, the uncaptured mouse keeps turning. Esc releases the cursor and pauses aim until you click the battlefield.</p><h3>Dash through the fight.</h3><p>Every mech has a damaging dash. Press Shift to dash in your movement direction, or along your aim when stationary. It deals 160 damage and staggers each enemy you pass through once, then recharges in 3 seconds. Your weapons pause during the dash. Solid terrain stops it. E uses your equipped special.</p><h3>Give each hand a job.</h3><p>Carbine and railgun reward hits on the upper quarter of enemy armor; gold damage numbers mark precision hits. Aim at the gold strip on practice targets. Rail shots also pierce and interrupt. Shotgun blasts have a tight center for mid-range hits and push back close enemies. Rockets gently track enemies near your aim when fired; sharp dodges and cover break guidance. Plasma builds three visible purple charge pips: the fourth hit causes a burst that interrupts nearby foes. Hits from teammates combine, but charges expire after 1.5 seconds without a hit. Gatling accuracy and fire rate build while held for 0.6 seconds. Flames leave a short burn, so you can ignite a group and attack with the other hand. The phaser trades damage for reliable beam tracking and repairs. Pair range with crowd control, or burst damage with sustain. No additional buttons are needed.</p><h3>Melee earns its slot.</h3><p>The laser sword deals 180 damage on contact and launches a wide 90-damage wave. A target hit by the blade does not also take wave damage. The plasma sledgehammer deals 300 on direct contact and releases a 220m radial blast that staggers targets; an aerial slam dives to the ground first. The pile lance delivers a 288-damage thrust at 200m and interrupts attacks. Shock claws cleave at 110m and restore 3 armor per connected swing, once even when several targets are hit. The scythe sweeps a 190m circle and pulls enemies 70m closer. Most weapons sustain 180–285 damage per second at their effective range. The phaser trades damage for healing; blast damage falls off away from a direct hit. Stunned enemies take normal damage.</p><p>Hold the button assigned to the Bulwark to raise it in front of you. Its plate covers 54% of the body's height and reduces covered frontal bullet hits by 80%. Your head, feet, sides, and back remain vulnerable. Releasing the button removes protection. Two shields do not multiply damage reduction. Your other hand remains usable.</p><h3>Read the hostile frame.</h3><p>Enemies commit to their warning. Leave charge lanes and amber impact circles; break a Needle’s sightline; use EMP, lance, rail or hammer to interrupt. Pale ground rings mark recovery openings. Green circles and open petals signal a Mender repairing another robot. Flight avoids ground stomps and artillery.</p>${Object.values(
        ENEMY_ROLES,
      )
        .filter((e) => e.counter)
        .map((e) => `<p><b>${e.name} / ${e.role}</b> · ${e.counter}</p>`)
        .join(
          '',
        )}<h3>Build your mech during the fight.</h3><p>Defeat hostiles and clear objectives to earn field XP. Each level offers three upgrades; choose with 1, 2 or 3 while moving and fighting. Choices stay banked until you select them. Press U or Esc to release the cursor and use the on-screen cards. Combat keeps running, including in co-op.</p><p>Explore for salvage caches and resonance relays. Approach a cache and press F to spend shared salvage on its displayed salvage tech. Link a resonance relay with F for its displayed support effect; some links also cost shared salvage. Each pilot makes personal upgrade choices and can link each relay once. B opens your field inventory, including stack counts and active relay timers. These systems apply immediately to your equipped weapons, special, movement and hull.</p><h3>Extract. Refit. Drop again.</h3><p>Play nine missions across three acts. Shared salvage also earns campaign refit choices after extraction. Install run modules before the next drop; they stack up to three times and last the run. Your field XP, upgrades and salvage tech carry through the campaign after extraction. Relay links and timed support reset with each sortie. Defeat or withdrawal ends the run; saved workshop mechs remain. Mission drills let you try each arena and its field systems without campaign rewards.</p><h3>Cinderfall · Operation 01</h3><p>Land, destroy shield relays and orbital batteries, recover six cells for the canyon crawler, break the reactor coolant nodes, defeat the warden, and extract. Walk or fly near a loose cell to carry it; approach the crawler to deliver. You can carry one cell at a time and still fight normally. A downed or disconnected pilot drops their cell. Checkpoints repair the squad. Two emergency redeploys recover a full squad wipe after seven seconds. Stay close to a downed ally for a free revive. Avoid damage for seven seconds to start slow hull repair. All surviving pilots must land on the extraction pad for six seconds once the ship arrives.</p><h3>Reports and suggestions.</h3><p>Press F8 or Report to capture the game and send a bug or suggestion to GitHub. Add text or an optional voice recording. Solo play pauses while reporting; co-op continues.</p><h3>Your test platform.</h3><p>Targets reset automatically. Try melee on the close target and wide attacks against the cluster. E uses your special; choose Repair field for healing. Click the railgun once: it charges automatically for 0.66 seconds, fires, then recovers for 0.5 seconds. Keep holding to repeat the full charge-and-recovery cycle. Releasing finishes the current charge but stops the next cycle. Dashing cancels a charge. The Dynamo cannon reloads through movement: boost, fly, or dash 500m to charge its next 280-damage shot. Its reticle ring shows charge. Standing still, aiming, falling, or pushing against a wall does not recharge it. Every equipped item adds weight. Mix five frame parts and paint each independently. Select Boosters to choose exhaust color.</p><p>Touch: left stick moves, drag to aim, hold LEFT HAND or RIGHT HAND to attack, and hold FLIGHT to rise. Keep the host tab active in co-op.</p>`,
    );
    $('#manualImpactMode').onclick = () => {
      toggleImpactMode();
      syncImpactMode();
    };
  }

  return showManual;
}
